==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Sir Metal Seal]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
All you need are 2-3 meatshields and 2-3 attackers for the peons and as many [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metals]] as possible for the Sir Metal Seals. [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] and [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]] like [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] and others are particularly useful for hitting the peons before they reach the frontlines.

While the alien supports seem to be hard to deal with, they are actually quite manageable. With there being no enemies over 201 range, [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] can easily deal with them thanks to his high damage and quick attack rate if you are doing your best to prevent the Sir Metal Seals from pushing.

On 4-Crown, it is possible to use a level 50 [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] (recommended to be talented, but not needed) to rush this stage. Send out [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellites]], have them take care of the Celeboodles, then send out Bahamut and spam all of your lineup to quickly destroy the enemy base before Sir Metal Seal manages to block the path.

